{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The process involved a comprehensive check of all draft application materials against the inventor's source disclosures.\n\nFirst, I constructed a complete source ledger by tracing every limitation in all 22 claims, every numbered part from 10 to 94 as listed in `draft/numerals.md`, and all specific structures described in the detailed description and abstract. Each feature—including the rail, the reversible fence mechanism with its screws and mounting holes, the two independent guide carriages with their keys, bushings, clamp knobs, and shoes, the pointers, distance marks, center index, sight notch, and the spacer plate—was successfully traced to an affirmative statement in `input/disclosure.md` or the USER passages of `input/conversation.md`.\n\nSecond, I reviewed the figure briefs for FIGs. 1-7. The descriptions of the parts and their relationships are consistent with the source disclosure. The use of \"shown schematically\" for generic shapes like the carriage bodies and fence is appropriate under the review instructions, as the claims and description remain shape-neutral and no unsupported technical function is added by the generic depiction.\n\nThird, I performed an internal consistency check. The terminology is used consistently throughout the claims, description, and figure briefs, adhering to the list in `input/brief.md`. Each reference numeral consistently refers to a single part. Cross-references for sectional views, such as lines 3-3 and 5-5, are correct and consistent between the drawing descriptions and the figure briefs. No drafting notes, placeholders, or unresolved issues were found in the text.\n\nThe entire review confirms that the draft is fully supported by the source material and is internally consistent. There are no findings to report."}
